WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:05.920
It's growing healthy.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.690
So cute!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.590
Kukuru-san, lunch break is almost over.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.280
Oh, okay.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.390
See you, Fuuka.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.370
Yeah.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.280
Bye-bye.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.870
Kukuru-san, do you still want 
to work as an attendant?

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.440
Why?

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.900
I mean... You were looking at the fish 
with your eyes glistening.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.740
I'm going to focus 
on marketing work for now.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:47.980
I'm going to focus...

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.030
<b>All staff welcome!!</b>

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.030
<b>Submit a big event idea!</b>

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.030
<b>Hope we get lots</b>

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.030
<b>Gain more fans 
of Tingarla's creatures!</b>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.200
She said it twice.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.290
Maeda-kun, your plan's been accepted.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.380
Huh?

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:31.260
The director was thoroughly impressed 
with your idea to have the staff cosplay as fish.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.300
Nice!

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.180
No way.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:38.670
Kudaka-kun, Plankton, you two take charge 
of setting up the cosplay event.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.680
Okay.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.370
Choose a representative from each department, 
assemble an executive team, and prepare—

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.600
Just a second!

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.560
What?

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.520
I think Maeda-san should take charge, 
since it's her idea.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.500
Maeda-kun's a part-timer.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.940
I can't have her do so much.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.630
I don't think it matters 
that she's part-time!

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.440
Plan a meeting for the event immediately.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.200
That's all from me.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.840
This doesn't make sense.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.350
It's fine.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.720
No, it's not.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.910
I really don't mind.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.040
But...

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.130
It's hard work making your
own plan come to life,

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.380
but when you're done, 
you don't even remember the hardships.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.050
You just end up happy 
having done it.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:26.830
Of course, I'll have your back 
all the way!

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:27.960
But...

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.770
I really love your idea!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.400
The staff members dress up as fish, 
and the guests guess the names of the fish.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.490
If they get it right, 
they get a fishy sticker,

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.910
<b>Fishy Stickers</b>

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.910
and once they've collected them all, 
they get a gift.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.910
We can get them interested in fish 
in a way that they'll enjoy.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.170
It's a great idea!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.320
Do you cosplay as a hobby, Akari-chan?

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.610
No, not at all.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.090
I just kinda came up with the idea 
when I saw that hat.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.530
Oh, I see.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.040
So I really didn't have any deep thoughts

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:06.110
about getting people 
to like animals or anything.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.760
I'm just a part-timer.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.060
It's not as if I'm enthusiastic about it, 
so don't worry about me.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.480
I'm not obsessed with aquariums 
the way you are, either.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.900
Okay, that's the end of my day.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.660
Good work, everyone.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.040
Good work.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.170
Good work.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.790
We don't have too much time.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.830
Let's contact all the departments and
get started with planning meetings tomorrow.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.160
Okay.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.630
Do you think I was being too pushy?

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.000
Akari-chan isn't the type 
to take it that way.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:43.960
Yeah...

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:49.450
Akari-chan isn't working at the aquarium 
because she's particularly interested in it.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.640
Yeah.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.110
I thought she was starting 
to like it a little, though.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:59.760
So I wanted to honor 
her cosplay event idea.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.650
I didn't especially like aquariums 
in the beginning, either.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.400
You're right.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.100
But after a while,

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:12.080
I started to enjoy taking care of the sea life 
and seeing the guests smile.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.480
And I started wanting 
to stay at the aquarium.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.120
Yeah.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.630
I think most people don't find work 
because it's what they love, the way you do.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.140
What I love? Well...

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.640
Can I vent a little?

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.770
Go ahead.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.460
I want to do attendant work!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.990
Venting over.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.800
Thanks for hearing me out.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:49.540
Yeah.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:56.040
The goal of the event is 
to gain more fans of Tingarla, right?

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:01.050
I want Akari-chan to like the animals 
even just a little more.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.280
You're right.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:19.070
Akari-chan, could you take this 
to the shop?

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.640
It got delivered here by mistake.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.020
Got it.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.990
Good job, Kaoru-chan.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:31.420
The guests loved it.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.830
The whiteys were especially eager today, huh?

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.580
They must be getting used 
to underwater feeding.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:41.130
I hope the sand tiger sharks become popular.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:42.970
They're pretty dull.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.060
Even though they're really cute.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.090
<b>Cosplay Event Meeting Agenda</b>

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.090
<b>In attendance (Attendants, Marketing, Facility)</b>

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.090
<b>Shimabukuro Kaoru, Yonekura Marina, 
Kudaka Karin, Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.960
Hey, hey, how about mermaids?

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:53.050
Mermaids, huh?

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.050
Yeah.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.670
Like these!

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.550
That's not the kind of cosplay 
we're doing, is it?

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.820
We're wearing fish costumes, 
aren't we?

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.580
That's my understanding.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.230
Yes, that's right.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.580
Oh, come on!

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.300
I don't think that fits 
the goal of the project.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.610
<b>Cosplay Event Meeting</b>

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.610
<b>Theme: Let's get people 
to appreciate the critters at Tingarla!</b>

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.000
Are you sure that's not just something 
you want to do, Marina-san?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.370
That's right!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.440
She admitted it.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:20.410
As a kid, I always wanted 
to become a mermaid when I grew up.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.430
I'm sure it'll be a hit!

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.250
That might be good.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.050
I think it'll get more people's
attention on the animals

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.270
if the whole event is more interesting.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.990
It should achieve the goal 
of the project, too.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:35.890
Right?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:39.980
But don't you think having mermaids 
among all the fish is a bit out of left field?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:45.360
Then how about we have all kinds 
of ocean-related cosplay and not just mermaids?

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.720
Awesome!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.280
That might work.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.920
That might be fun for the customers.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.610
What do you think, Maeda-san?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.600
Huh?

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:56.350
It won't be exactly what
we had in mind in the beginning.

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.640
Oh, right.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.120
Sea-themed cosplay. Right.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.640
Can it be anything as long as 
it has to do with the sea?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:06.680
Is there something you want 
to cosplay as, Kaoru-san?

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.000
What is it?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.420
I think you'd look awesome 
in cosplay, Kaoru-san.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.040
Let's get the cosplay event details 
out of the way.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:18.760
Okay.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.310
We need to order costumes 
and stickers and stuff, too.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.680
We're going to be busy.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.590
It's Udon-chan.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:25.630
What's she saying?

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.400
She says she used our feedback the other day 
to improve the menu items.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.760
She wants us to come try it out.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.280
Want to swing by 
on our way home today?

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.510
I can't go today.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.000
The assistant director asked me 
to prepare the documents.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.240
Ah.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.450
Want to come with me, then, Akari-chan?

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.160
Okay.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.780
I changed the flavoring and stuff.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:56.280
They said they'll put it on the
restaurant menu if it turns out good.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.390
That's amazing!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.300
It's thanks to all of you.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.770
I'd appreciate it if you can give me 
your opinions again.

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:04.030
Okay.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.920
Take your time.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.850
Let's dig in, then.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:08.490
Okay.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:09.820
Thanks for the food.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.000
She made the sandwiches easier to eat.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.660
It's cuter looking than before, too.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.790
Do you think I did something wrong 
to Kukuru-san?

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:29.270
I turned her down after she offered 
to let me lead the project.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:34.300
I thought you invited me today 
to talk about that.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.080
No way.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.260
I just felt like chatting 
over some good food.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.630
Okay.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.840
You've been working with us 
quite a bit, Akari-chan.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.100
Are you able to keep up with college?

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.640
I manage to make things work.

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:53.960
I even find time 
to hang out with friends.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.020
All right.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.200
Recommendations? Well, then...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:03.340
The Ohana Barbecue set comes with a sauce 
that has plenty of pineapple!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.120
Give it a try!

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.200
One of those, then.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.160
Thank you!

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.110
I've only ever watched 
at the cultural festivals and stuff at school.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.920
I never participate.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.470
Really?

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:20.010
You switched jobs because you wanted 
to work at an aquarium, right?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:20.910
Yeah.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.510
It was my dream to become
an attendant since I was a kid.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:30.090
I don't have any preferences of any sort.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.730
So there isn't any particular job 
that I want to do, either.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.790
Here's your Piña Colada and Blue Hawaii.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:53.920
For the fish to cosplay as,

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.340
I've chosen the sand tiger shark, 
giant manta ray, green sea turtle,

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:01.640
amethyst anthias, pyramid butterflyfish, 
moon jellyfish, flashlight fish,

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.150
<b>Giant manta ray</b>

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.130
<b>Green sea turtle</b>

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:04.430
<b>Amethyst anthias</b>

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:04.430
<b>Pyramid butterflyfish</b>

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:04.430
<b>Moon jellyfish</b>

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:04.430
<b>Flashlight fish</b>

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.430
<b>Four-stripe damselfish</b>

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.430
and the four-stripe damselfish.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.080
Looks good.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.040
Great.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.630
I'm glad I worked on it with Kai-kun.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.450
Thanks, both of you.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:12.310
Not at all.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:16.320
We of the fish team would like 
to be the ones to dress up.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.650
About that...

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.150
May we not?

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:25.830
Actually, I want to ask you guys for a favor.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.160
Urashima Tarou?

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.180
Yeah.

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:36.630
I want the whole fish team 
to do Urashima Tarou cosplay.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.580
Pass.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.930
Tell us, Kaoru-chan!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.930
I loved the story 
of Urashima Tarou as a kid.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:49.430
<b>Urashima Tarou</b>

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.870
I wanted to go to Ryugu Castle.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.690
That's how I started wanting 
to work at an aquarium.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.620
Uh...

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.970
What does that have to do 
with cosplaying?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:03.510
I thought it might be a good way 
to get kids hooked on fish.

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.910
You're Urashima Tarou, then, Kaoru-chan.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.290
So you're on board?

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:13.280
I'd like to be a flashlight fish 
instead of a seabream.

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.040
I think Kai-kun should be 
a pyramid butterflyfish.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:16.960
Why, though?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.370
Kuuya would be a green sea turtle.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:23.260
Which would mean that Umi-yan-san is...

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:28.530
<b>When The Light Shines</b>

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.830
Oh, crap...

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:31.020
<b>When The Light Shines</b>

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.170
The mermaid costumes arrived.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.530
Could we take a look?

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.020
Okay!

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:47.260
Let's try them on later.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:48.360
Okay.

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:50.700
Wow.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.620
Are we actually wearing those?

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.040
Of course.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.200
I'm not wearing that.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:58.970
All three of us should wear it.

00:12:58.970 --> 00:12:59.720
No.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:00.750
Shizuku's coming.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.810
I can't be dressed like that.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.280
Shizu-kun's coming!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.340
Yay!

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.880
He says he's going to

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:12.390
get everything on the quiz right 
and win tons of fishy stickers.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.030
Really?

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:16.060
All right, let's make it good.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.360
Shimabukuro-san.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.320
I put the costumes for the event 
in the attendants' room.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.110
Could you take a look later?

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.610
Got it.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:33.310
The fish look as good as ever.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.120
I'm not sure about that.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:39.700
Animals often hide it 
when they're not feeling well.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.250
We have to keep our eyes open 
for the slightest changes.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:47.260
I always worry that they might die 
before I notice.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:55.230
I delivered the costumes 
to Shimabukuro's fish team.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.680
Thanks.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.430
Look, look.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:00.320
Pirates, huh?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.190
I thought I'd wear this.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.450
Looks good.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.240
You should dress up with us.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.240
I'll pass.

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:09.000
Yeah?

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.620
I have to clean all this up.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.840
That's your day, Akari-chan.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:16.620
Right.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.190
Good work today.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.500
Good work.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.300
<b>Teruya Tsukimi</b>

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:34.960
Yes?

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:36.700
<i>Hello, Akari-chan?</i>

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:37.810
<i>Do you have a minute?</i>

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.750
Yes.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.830
I just got off work.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:44.160
<i>They're putting my sandwich 
on the menu!</i>

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.650
Really?

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.550
<i>I got approval for something
I came up with for the first time.</i>

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:50.090
<i>It's all thanks 
to the advice you gave me.</i>

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:52.970
It's all thanks 
to the advice you gave me.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.080
Thanks.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.140
<i>Nah.</i>

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.320
<i>Hey, Tsukimi-san...</i>

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:01.990
I guess work gets complicated, 
even if you're doing what you love, huh?

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:07.960
I've always thought that people 
who do what they love are all just having fun.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.740
But I guess

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>it's not all fun.</i>

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.850
I guess.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:16.720
It can get pretty miserable.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.660
Thank you.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.080
I'll come by the shop 
sometime again.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.230
<i>Sure.</i>

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:25.910
<i>Bye.</i>

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.250
Of course.

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.130
Of course it would.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.930
<b>Fish Cosplay Event</b>

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:51.930
<b>Find the sea creatures and win a plushie!</b>

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.930
<b>Starting Tomorrow!</b>

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.970
Hello.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:59.500
I brought the stickers 
to hand out to guests tomorrow.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.070
Thank you.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:02.780
Tomorrow's the day, huh?

00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:03.850
Yes.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.440
What? I'm a sand tiger shark?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:07.570
Yes.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.690
All right, all right. 
Sounds good.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.800
See you tomorrow.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:13.760
See you then.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.530
I've delivered them.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.000
Thanks!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.410
Kukuru.

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.750
They're telling me they still
haven't gotten the fishy stickers.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:23.840
Oh, no!

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:28.390
I left my order email in the "Drafts"
folder and forgot to send it!

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:32.120
We won't get them by tomorrow 
if we order them now.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.480
What do we do?

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:37.130
I was going to check the art 
one more time before I sent it.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:39.640
Let's ditch the stickers.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:46.150
How about we switch to putting stamps 
on the tickets when they get questions right?

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.490
What are we going to do for stamps?

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:52.140
I think we can avoid a lot of trouble 
if we use the stamps from the shop.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.850
That's a good idea.

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:56.450
They aren't the right species
 of fish, though.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:01.390
Also, Chiyu-san said 
Shizu-kun's looking forward to the stickers.

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:04.710
I'm sure he's not the only kid who is.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.940
I don't want to let them down.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:09.580
But we won't get them 
in time for tomorrow.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:12.000
Let's explain and try to
have them understand.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.090
I'm going to make them!

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:17.090
I've made hand-made stickers before.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.300
I can get them done by tomorrow.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:22.550
All right.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.690
Akari-chan, the time.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.910
Didn't you have plans 
with someone today?

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:31.580
It's going to get busy tomorrow, 
but we're counting on you.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:32.320
Right.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.530
Good work, everyone.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.100
Good work.

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.700
Sorry for imposing, 
but please let me do this.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:40.840
I want everyone to enjoy the event.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.700
Yeah, let's do it!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.470
<b></b>

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>Sorry, something came up. Raincheck today? 
I promise I'll make it up to you!</b>

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>Forgive me, sire</b>

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.980
We have art assets.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.930
We can make the files based on these.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.000
Akari-chan?

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.120
Did you forget something?

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:19.370
My plans with my friend got canceled.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.370
So I'm going to help out.

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:23.370
But...

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.120
I won't have anything 
to do at home anyway.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.870
It'll be a nice change of pace.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.340
I might like seeing the guests happy, too.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:34.990
Okay!

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:37.010
Let's make sure they enjoy it!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.000
What should I do?

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:45.070
Could you resize these assets 
to fit standard paper size?

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:46.380
Got it.

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:48.460
We'll pay you for your time.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:49.850
I'm going to go buy the sheets!

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.290
Four-stripe damselfish?

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:10.570
Yup.

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.490
See how it has four black stripes?

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:18.280
There's also a two-stripe damselfish 
and a three-stripe damselfish.

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:19.800
Huh.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.140
<b>Starting Today!</b>

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.140
<b>Fish Cosplay Event</b>

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.140
<b>Find the sea creatures and win a plushie!</b>

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:33.900
The aquarium staff will be dressing up 
as all kinds of fish today.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.400
Pick them out and guess their names!

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:41.800
But be careful, 
because some of them aren't fish.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.530
There, there.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.610
I'm a peaceful shark.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:51.500
You don't have to cry, do you?

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.500
<b>Ryugu Castle</b>

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:00.010
Urashima Tarou's the best!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:01.610
Thank you.

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.080
In place of seabream and halibut,

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:07.720
we present to you the dance of the
amethyst anthias and pyramid butterflyfish.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.140
Bravo!

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:17.820
Weird.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:24.860
Nice effort!

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.210
Why, thank you.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.500
This is kind of embarrassing.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.240
You're so cute, Fuuka!

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.380
<i>Qué linda!</i>

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.260
Mommy, you're so pretty.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.490
Yeah?

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:43.240
Yeah.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.660
The Little Mermaid!

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:47.890
You look good, too, Shizu-kun.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:52.730
Hello, Shizu-kun.

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:56.090
Four strike dangerfish!

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:56.880
Hm?

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:57.840
Close enough.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:58.820
Bingo!

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.270
Here you go, a sticker.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:03.700
Thank you!

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:05.710
Mommy, a sticker!

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:07.470
Good for you, Shizu-kun.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:08.070
Yeah!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.150
Staying behind late to make them 
was totally worth it, huh?

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:13.080
Yeah.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.790
Oh, look.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.940
Four-stripe damselfish.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.760
They're so cute!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:26.470
Look!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.510
Looks like Tingarla 
has a new marine-life fan.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.610
Is there something 
you want to say to me?

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:48.490
N-No...

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.160
We're opening a new area 
next spring to commemorate

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.920
the one-year anniversary 
of the aquarium.

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:37.390
You're in charge of it, Plankton.
